00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:03.760 align:start position:0%
us-russia tensions are rising this  morning after the Trump administration  officially backed out of a cold war arms  treaty withdrawal from a landmark  nuclear missile pact is raising fears of  a new arms race the u.s. accuses Russia  of violating the INF treaty by  developing banned weapons Russia denies  it the treaty prohibits  intermediate-range land-based missiles  it was signed in 1987 by President  Ronald Reagan and Soviet leader Mikhail  Gorbachev the u.s. also may remove  thousands of US troops from Afghanistan  as part of a deal to end America's  longest war ever sources tell CBS News  the Trump administration is prepared to  reduce troop levels in Afghanistan from  about 14,000 to between 8 and 9 thousand  it would be part of a possible peace  agreement with the Taliban the u.s.  peace envoy to Afghanistan hinted  earlier this week a deal possibly could  be reached during upcoming talks in  Qatar two US soldiers were killed in  Afghanistan this week private first  class Brendan crusher of Stryker Ohio  and specialist Michael Nance of Chicago  are among 15 US troops who have died in  Afghanistan this year
 

